UNIT isPrimitive
KIND FUNCTIONAL
ORACLE-CLASS deterministic
SIG isPrimitive(val: any) -> boolean
DEPENDS-ON none

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BEHAVIOR  (exact, complete — transcribed from the verified source, ordered)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The unit is a single pure predicate. The SOURCE implements it with this
# EXACT two-branch structure (do NOT re-derive a different-but-"equivalent"
# boolean expression that diverges on the exotic typeof cases below):
#
#   BRANCH 1:  if (typeof val === 'object')
#                  return (val === null)        # true ONLY for null; false for every other object
#   BRANCH 2:  return (typeof val !== 'function')
#
# Read as prose:
#   - Compute t = typeof val   (the JS `typeof` operator).
#   - If t === 'object': the value is a non-null object reference UNLESS it is
#     literally `null` (because `typeof null === 'object'` in JS). So return
#     true iff val === null, else false.
#   - Otherwise (t is anything except 'object'): return true UNLESS t === 'function'.
#     I.e. function values are the only non-'object' typeof that is NOT a primitive.
#
# Equivalent closed form for the SAME observable result on ALL JS values:
#     result = (typeof val === 'object') ? (val === null) : (typeof val !== 'function')
#
# IMPORTANT NUANCE — why the branch ORDER must be preserved:
#   The hint's flat form `val == null || (typeof val !== 'object' && typeof val !== 'function')`
#   yields the SAME result for every value class in this generator's scope, but the
#   AUTHORITATIVE definition is the branch structure above. The one JS value where a
#   naive simplification could diverge is the legacy browser `document.all` object,
#   for which `typeof document.all === 'undefined'` yet it is an object: under the
#   source's BRANCH structure it falls through to BRANCH 2 and returns true
#   (typeof is 'undefined', not 'function'). `document.all` is NOT constructible in
#   Node and is OUT-OF-ENVELOPE here (see SCOPE) — documented for completeness so a
#   blind re-emitter reproduces the branch logic, not a lookalike.
#
# The `typeof` operator's value classification (the full mapping this predicate keys on):
#   typeof null        === 'object'    -> BRANCH 1 -> val===null -> TRUE
#   typeof <plain obj> === 'object'    -> BRANCH 1 -> val!==null -> FALSE
#   typeof <array>     === 'object'    -> BRANCH 1 -> FALSE
#   typeof <Map/Set/Date/RegExp/Buffer/Uint8Array/boxed-wrapper> === 'object' -> FALSE
#   typeof undefined   === 'undefined' -> BRANCH 2 -> 'undefined' !== 'function' -> TRUE
#   typeof <string>    === 'string'    -> BRANCH 2 -> TRUE
#   typeof <number>    === 'number'    -> BRANCH 2 -> TRUE  (incl. NaN, Infinity, -Infinity, 0, -0)
#   typeof <boolean>   === 'boolean'   -> BRANCH 2 -> TRUE
#   typeof <bigint>    === 'bigint'    -> BRANCH 2 -> TRUE
#   typeof <symbol>    === 'symbol'    -> BRANCH 2 -> TRUE       (see SCOPE: out-of-envelope for the codec)
#   typeof <function>  === 'function'  -> BRANCH 2 -> 'function' !== 'function' -> FALSE  (out-of-envelope)
#
# No exceptions are thrown for any input. No mutation. No side effects.
# Calling with zero args: `val` is `undefined` -> TRUE (same as passing undefined).
# `-0` (negative zero): typeof is 'number' -> TRUE (identical to +0).
# Boxed wrappers new Number(1) / new String("x") / new Boolean(true): typeof is
#   'object' and they are not null -> FALSE. (Distinct from their primitive forms,
#   which are TRUE.) This boxed-vs-primitive split is the classic gotcha and is
#   exercised in the generator's curated prefix.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPECTED RESULT TABLE  (self-consistent with genInputs — every value class the
# generator can emit appears here with its exact boolean)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   TRUE  (primitive):
#     null
#     undefined            (and the zero-arg call)
#     ""  and any string
#     0, 1, -1, -0, 3.14, any finite/integer number
#     NaN
#     Infinity, -Infinity
#     true, false
#     any bigint           (e.g. 0n, 10n, -7n, very-large)
#   FALSE (non-primitive):
#     {}  and any plain object
#     []  and any array (including [] empty)
#     new Map(), new Set()
#     new RegExp("..") and /regex/ literal
#     new Date()  (revived as a non-null plain object via codec; result FALSE either way)
#     Buffer.from(..), new Uint8Array(..) (any TypedArray / ArrayBuffer view)
#     new Number(1), new String("x"), new Boolean(true)   (boxed wrappers)
#   TRUE  (out-of-envelope but defined for the blind re-emitter; NOT codec-faithful,
#          so NOT emitted by genInputs — see SCOPE):
#     any Symbol  -> TRUE
#   FALSE (out-of-envelope; not emitted):
#     any function (declaration, arrow, class, async, generator) -> FALSE

ORACLE value -> oracle.json

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCOPE
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IN-CONTRACT LOGIC (reproduce exactly): the entire predicate. It is the pure
#   two-branch typeof test described in BEHAVIOR. There is no option, no config,
#   no carried data, no dependency. The full behavior is defined above for every
#   value class — a blind re-emitter needs nothing else.
#
# CARRIED DATA: none.
#
# OUT-OF-ENVELOPE (behavior fully DEFINED above, but NOT emitted by genInputs
#   because the value cannot cross the oracle's JSON+tag codec by value/identity;
#   a blind re-emitter still reconstructs the result from this spec):
#   - Symbol values: typeof 'symbol' -> BRANCH 2 -> TRUE. The harness codec has
#     NO tag for symbols (supported tags: undef/regex/bigint/num/boxed/set/map/u8),
#     so a Symbol cannot be persisted into the held-out set; emitting one would
#     poison the held-out. Behavior is nonetheless pinned: ALL symbols -> TRUE.
#   - Function values: typeof 'function' -> BRANCH 2 -> FALSE. No codec tag for a
#     live function; not emitted. Behavior pinned: ALL functions -> FALSE.
#   - `document.all` (legacy browser host object): typeof === 'undefined' though it
#     is an object; the source returns TRUE for it (BRANCH 2). Not constructible in
#     Node; never emitted. Documented only to justify the branch order.
#
# OUT-OF-CONTRACT (stateful mutators / side APIs): none — the unit is pure.

